  "notes": [
    "Planet discs are labelled observation models for teaching; they do not represent seeing a second Moon or Mars from their own surface.",
    "Rover chassis stays intact. Animate the small hubs on the common original canvas and translate forward facing right; do not mesh-deform or separate suspension.",
    "Lunar rover shows two near-side and two far-side wheels; Mars rover shows three near-side with far-side wheels partially occluded.",
    "The lunar section is airless: use optional music rather than fictional ambient wind or audible travel sounds.",
    "Background sources native 2172x724. Transparent sprites retain complete original alpha/camera canvases without individual silhouette alignment."
